      "skos:prefLabel": "FIPS 200",
      "skos:definition": "Federal Information Processing Standard 200, the NIST standard that sets minimum security requirements in 17 security-related areas for federal information systems and directs agencies to meet them by selecting the NIST SP 800-53 control baseline matching the system's FIPS 199 impact level; the bridge between categorization and the control baselines behind FedRAMP authorizations of services such as Salesforce Government Cloud Plus.",
      "kto:domain": "public-sector-and-compliance",
