      "skos:definition": "The risk that data held in a Salesforce org is accessed, exported or disclosed by someone not authorized to have it — today most often through stolen credentials, social engineering or compromised integration tokens rather than platform flaws. Under the shared responsibility model, reducing it is largely a customer configuration task.",
